	(text "U18 ASIC_REF_VCM 0.75 V"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 310.44 421.9 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.2 1.2)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "eabdd4e6-3956-5710-8664-a98a86029014")
	)
	(text_box "1. Function: Seven regulators make the ASIC rails from +3V3; each rail is shared by all eight ASICs through the two ASIC ports. LT3042 (U12 VDD_FE, U16 REF_VDD, U18 REF_VCM 0.75 V): Vout = 100 uA x RSET. TPS7A2015 (U13 VDD_ADC, U14 VDD_DRIVER, U15 DVDD, U17 VDD_CGEN): fixed 1.50 V. All start from EN_ASIC_RAILS (TPS7A20 EN high above 0.9 V max, LT3042 EN/UV above about 1.24 V). R802 (47k to AGND) is the minimum load of U18.\n\n2. Source / changes: LT3042 cells inherited from Gerald LDO Board A (Reference/LDO Board A/PCB.kicad_sch): IN, EN/UV and PGFB at the input, ILIM to ground, OUT=OUTS, CIN/COUT 10 uF 10 V 0603, CSET 1 uF, PG open, RSET 15k/7.5k; ADI LT3042 data sheet (revision letter not recorded; edition at the URL accessed 24 Nov 2026), Typical Application p.1 and Pin Functions, https://www.analog.com/media/en/technical-documentation/data-sheets/lt3042.pdf. Claude changes: EN/UV to EN_ASIC_RAILS; one regulator per rail for eight ASICs. V24 (Howard, 8 Nov 2026, \"find smaller parts\"): U13/U14/U15/U17 changed from LT3042 3x3 DFN cells to TI TPS7A2015PDQNR 1x1 mm X2SON (TI SBVS338H Rev H, Jul 2024: Pin Functions p.4 DQN 1 OUT/2 GND/3 EN/4 IN/5 pad; Recommended Operating Conditions p.5 CIN 1 uF, COUT 1-200 uF with >= 0.47 uF effective; Electrical Characteristics p.7 VEN(HI) 0.9 V max; https://www.ti.com/lit/ds/symlink/tps7a20.pdf); their RSET/CSET (R301-R701, C303-C703) are removed and CIN/COUT are 1 uF 10 V 0402. Trade-off: 7 uVrms against 0.8 uVrms (LT3042), accepted by Gerald 9 Nov 2026 (\"I think its okay to do that\"). V34 (12 Nov 2026): every regulator now returns to the ground its rail is decoupled to on the ASIC boards: U13 (VDD_ADC) with C301/C302 moved from GND to AGND, and U15 (DVDD) with C501/C502 moved from AGND to GND; the other five were already on AGND. Basis: ASIC boards V6 decouple DVDD to DGND (C7, C14, C61, C62) and every other rail to AGND (read from both V6 board files, 12 Nov 2026); meeting with the ASIC designer, 12 Nov 2026 (2026-11-12_FPGA_Work/07_Meeting_With_ASIC_Designer_V1/MEETING_NOTES_V1.md), answer B3 (two grounds, joined at one point on this board); review items LDOA-11 and LDOA-16. REF_VCM stays LT3042 because 0.75 V is below the TPS7A20 0.8 V minimum. Loads of REF_VDD/REF_VCM unknown. V36 (Howard, 16 Nov 2026, review item SYS-61 / fix P1, \"as long as it does not change the size\"): 0.6 mm test pads TP11, TP12, TP14-TP17 on VDD_FE, VDD_ADC, DVDD, REF_VDD, VDD_CGEN, REF_VCM. V37 (layout V18): TP13 (VDD_DRIVER), TP18 (VDD10), TP19 (VSS10) dropped, no room in the outline; probe C402, C902, C1002 instead. V41 (19 Nov 2026, pre-fabrication review V2 and Zitong Xu): R802 47k 1 % 0402 (Uniroyal 0402WGF4702TCE, JLC C25792, 4,838,934 orderable, read 19 Nov 2026 07:48 CST) added from ASIC_REF_VCM to AGND: 0.75 V / 47k = 16 uA, above the 10 uA minimum load the LT3042 needs for stability when VOUT is below 1 V (same data sheet, Electrical Characteristics, Minimum Load Required and Note 13, p.5). Designed by Claude; not in the inherited or data-sheet circuit. Unverified: the REF_VCM current of the ASIC itself and the output noise with this load. Carrier V7 (Claude, 24 Nov 2026): copied from FPGA-LDO A V24 / schematic V43 with values, footprints and LCSC numbers unchanged; refs U2-U8 -> U12-U18 (support parts keep their V24 numbers: C201-C203/R201 belong to U12, C301/C302 to U13, C401/C402 to U14, C501/C502 to U15, C601-C603/R601 to U16, C701/C702 to U17, C801-C803/R801/R802 to U18); V24 net VIN_3V3 is the carrier +3V3; the rail labels are global labels to the router plugs J5/J6 (sheet Router_Interface), where the 17 x 1 uF port capacitors sit. Schematic V2 (Claude, 24 Nov 2026, part choice approved by Howard): U13/U14/U15/U17 TPS7A2015PDQNR X2SON-4 1x1 mm (JLC C2862700, 1 orderable against 20 needed, read 24 Nov 2026, 18:33 CST) -> TI TPS7A2015PDBVR SOT-23-5 (JLC C2877859, 467 orderable, read 25 Nov 2026, 07:22 CST), the same TI regulator and 1.50 V option in its DBV package. Pins renumbered from TI SBVS338H Rev H (Jul 2024) p.4, Figure 4-4 and Pin Functions X2SON/SOT-23: IN 4 -> 1, GND 2 -> 2, EN 3 -> 3, OUT 1 -> 5, N/C pin 4 left open (no internal connection), DQN thermal pad 5 dropped (GND stays on pin 2); every net, R/C value and support part is unchanged. Symbol Carrier_V7_Local:TPS7A20_DBV (the V24 drawing with DBV numbers); footprint KiCad 10 stock Package_TO_SOT_SMD:SOT-23-5 copied to Carrier_V7_Local. DBV differences in the same data sheet: output tolerance +/-40 mV below 2.8 V out (p.6; DQN +/-30 mV), load regulation 19 mV (p.6; DQN 13 mV), dropout 205 mV max at 300 mA (p.6), RthJA 187.1 C/W (p.6; DQN 166.1). Unverified: rail loads, so U13-U15/U17 dissipation is not checked; the 40 mV tolerance against the ASIC supply limits. Schematic V4 (25 Nov 2026): unified 11 x 1 uF 0402 regulator caps (C203, C301-C803) from C14445 (10 V Extended) to C52923 (Samsung CL05A105KA5NQNC 1 uF 25 V Basic, same 0402 land, matching C51-C67); added TP13 on ASIC_VDD_DRIVER."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
