	(text_box "1. Function: U19 (LT3042) makes ASIC_VDD10 = +8.06 V from STIM_PRE_POS; U20 (LT3094) makes ASIC_VSS10 = -8.06 V from STIM_PRE_NEG (the net names are kept from the +/-10 V revisions). Both are referenced to AGND and start with EN_ASIC_RAILS. Each serves the stimulators of all eight ASICs (about 8 mA at Gerald's 2 mA per board maximum).\n\n2. Source / changes: U19 inherits Gerald LDO Board A U8 (LT3042, RSET 90k, input from an external INPUT_VDD10); U20 replaces LDO A U9 with a true negative LDO. ADI LT3042 data sheet (revision letter not recorded; edition at the URL accessed 24 Nov 2026), p.1 Features and Typical Application, p.3 Electrical Characteristics, https://www.analog.com/media/en/technical-documentation/data-sheets/lt3042.pdf ; ADI LT3094 data sheet Rev 0 (2018), p.1 and p.4, Pin Functions p.15, https://www.analog.com/media/en/technical-documentation/data-sheets/lt3094.pdf . Both set the output as 100 uA x RSET (SET pin current 100 uA, +/-1 % initial; output range 0 to 15 V and 0 to -19.5 V). Changed from the data sheet p.1 circuits: RSET 80.6k (was 33.2k), CSET 1 uF (was 4.7 uF); PGFB to IN, ILIM to ground, PG and VIOC open; EN/UV from EN_ASIC_RAILS. V34 (Howard, 12 Nov 2026: stimulation rails +/-8 V, the level the ASIC designer runs from a battery; meeting with the ASIC designer, 12 Nov 2026 (2026-11-12_FPGA_Work/07_Meeting_With_ASIC_Designer_V1/MEETING_NOTES_V1.md), answer B4): R901/R1001 changed from 100k to 80.6k 1 % 0402, Uniroyal 0402WGF8062TCE, JLC C25921 (124,346 orderable, JLC stock read 12 Nov 2026, 19:37 CST); 100 uA x 80.6k = 8.06 V. An exact 80.0k 0402 is not in JLC stock. With 1 % parts and 1 % SET current the rails lie between about 7.9 and 8.2 V. Checks for 8 V: U11 is the fixed LT3582-12 and stays at +/-12 V (factory set, data sheet 3582512fb p.1), so each LDO has about 3.9 V of headroom against a dropout of 350 mV (LT3042) and 235 mV (LT3094) and inputs far inside 20 V; the extra loss is about 4 V x 8 mA = 32 mW per regulator. The 0.8 uVrms (10 Hz-100 kHz) noise figure is specified for 1.3 V <= VOUT <= 15 V and -19.5 V <= VOUT <= -1.5 V with CSET 4.7 uF, so it does not depend on the 8 V setting; here CSET stays 1 uF. Output capacitors unchanged (C902 22 uF 25 V 1206; C1002 22 uF 1206 plus C1004 10 uF 25 V 0805; LT3042 needs >= 4.7 uF, LT3094 >= 10 uF). Unverified: noise measured at the ASIC pins; effective capacitance from the Samsung DC-bias curves at 8 V; no clamp or bleed on the rails at power-down (review items LDOA-08, -09, -28: not changed in V34). Carrier V7 (Claude, 24 Nov 2026): copied unchanged; refs U9/U10 -> U19/U20 (R901/R1001, C901-C903, C1001-C1004 keep their numbers); ASIC_VDD10/VSS10 are global labels to the router plugs. Schematic V4 (25 Nov 2026): added TP18 (ASIC_VDD10 +8.06 V) and TP19 (ASIC_VSS10 -8.06 V) so all 9 regulated ASIC rails are probeable."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
