		(uuid "958cd2d8-73d3-5518-813d-fcbaf7a3898f")
	)
	(text_box "1. Function: +3V3 from the carrier TPS54429E buck (sheet XEM_Power_USB, U1) feeds the stimulation converter U11 and the ASIC-rail regulators U12-U20; C43 decouples it at this block (C42 is DNP). R29/C44 delay EN_ASIC_RAILS by about 23 ms after ASIC_EN_SRC rises; ASIC_EN_SRC comes from U21 (block on the right), so the delay starts only after the XEM8305 power-good, which also enables VCCO. D13/R34 empty C44 in about 2 ms when ASIC_EN_SRC falls. TP31 (+3V3), TP34 (EN_ASIC_RAILS), TP35 (GND) and TP36 (AGND) are probe pads; the flag marks AGND (GND is flagged on sheet XEM_Power_USB). AGND and GND join only at NT1 on sheet Router_Interface.\n\n2. Source / changes: Copied from FPGA-LDO A V24 / schematic V43 (19 Nov 2026), block VIN_3V3 ENTRY, DELAYED ENABLE, RETURN BOND (Claude design, no manufacturer reference circuit). Delay: tau = R29 x C44 = 47 ms; LT3094 EN/UV turns on at 1.26 V, t = 47 ms x ln(3.3/2.04) = 23 ms (ADI LT3094 Rev 0, Electrical Characteristics p.4, https://www.analog.com/media/en/technical-documentation/data-sheets/lt3094.pdf); TPS7A20 VEN(HI) 0.9 V max (TI SBVS338H Rev H, p.7, https://www.ti.com/lit/ds/symlink/tps7a20.pdf). Changed for Carrier V7 by Claude: net VIN_3V3 is the carrier +3V3 (labels replaced by +3V3 symbols; on V24 it came from Frontend J2.68-70); refs C1/C2/C3/R1 -> C42/C43/C44/R29 and TP1/TP4/TP5/TP6 -> TP31/TP34/TP35/TP36 (clash with Carrier V6 refs); review fixes 24 Nov 2026: R29 pin 1 moved from +3V3 to ASIC_EN_SRC (U21), D13 + R34 added across R29, and C42 (22 uF entry bulk) set DNP because the buck output capacitors are on the same net: with C42 the +3V3 net held about 109.5 uF nominal, without it about 87.5 uF, against 22-68 uF for 3.3 V out in TI TPS54429E SLVSAS0 (Feb 2011, the edition TI serves at the URL, read 24 Nov 2026) p.14 Table 1 Recommended Component Values, https://www.ti.com/lit/ds/symlink/tps54429e.pdf ; NT1 moved to Router_Interface (same part, still the single bond); V24 GND flag not copied; C42/C43 voltage fields corrected to the JLC parts (C602037 25 V, C307331 50 V). Unverified: +3V3 stability with about 87.5 uF (load-step test on the first build; schematic V2 sets L1 to the TI table 2.2 uH); rail start order not measured."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
