	(text_box "1. Function: U21 (single buffer on +3V3) turns the 1.8 V XEM8305 power-good \"XEM PG\" (MC1.90, which also enables the VCCO regulator U2 on sheet XEM_Power_USB) into the 3.3 V source ASIC_EN_SRC of the R29/C44 delay, so the ASIC rails start about 23 ms after VCCO and never before it; when PG falls, U21 pulls ASIC_EN_SRC low and C44 empties through D13 and R34 in about 2 ms, so the rails stop with VCCO and the ASIC outputs and R19 cannot feed unpowered XEM banks. C68 decouples U21.\n\n2. Source / changes: Designed by Claude, 24 Nov 2026 (review fix, no manufacturer reference circuit); replaces the V24 tie of R29 pin 1 to +3V3. TI SN74LV1T34 data sheet SCLS743E (Dec 2013, revised Feb 2024): pins p.4 (1 NC, 2 A, 3 GND, 4 Y, 5 VCC), VIH 1.39 V max at VCC 3-3.3 V p.6, IO 25 mA and IOK 20 mA abs. max p.5, https://www.ti.com/lit/ds/symlink/sn74lv1t34.pdf ; Opal Kelly, Powering the XEM8305 (PG is a 1.8 V signal; power VCCO only after the FPGA rails are good), https://docs.opalkelly.com/xem8305/powering-the-xem8305/ (accessed 24 Nov 2026). Parts: U21 SN74LV1T34DBVR C100024 (20400 orderable), D13 = the V24 D11 part B0540WS-TP C668860 (5322), R34 470R 1% Uniroyal 0402WGF4700TCE, JLC Basic C25117 (1,792,699 orderable, read 25 Nov 2026 22:05 CST; schematic V8: was 220R C25091, which let U21 sink about 14 mA; 470R keeps the discharge near 5.5 mA, inside U21's 7 mA recommended output current, TI SCLS743E p.5, https://www.ti.com/lit/ds/symlink/sn74lv1t34.pdf), C68 100 nF C1525 (23031222); JLC read 25 Nov 2026, 07:22 CST. Symbol: KiCad 10 stock 74LVC1G34 (same DBV pinout) copied to project library Carrier_V7_Local; footprint KiCad 10 stock SOT-23-5, copied project-local. Unverified: PG state while the module is unpowered, and the real start and stop order on hardware."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
